    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d167">

                <pb facs="0332" n="244" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg244"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/2842: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Sofia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Murphy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi><anchor n="4" xml:id="d167-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sofia</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-29">November 29,
                            1918</date>.<lb/>[Received December 1—4:58 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>190. Prime Minister informs me Roumanian troops crossed river Danube last night,
                    search-lights having been used on Roumanian side. As population Toulcha greatly
                    disquieted, Prime Minister asks that United States intervene that terms
                    armistice be strictly adhered to.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Murphy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d167-f1" n="4" type="source" xml:id="d167-f1-content">
                <p>Forwarded to Colonel House as Department’s telegram No. 132, Dec. 6, 1918, 3
                    p.m.</p>
            </note>
